## Ideas evaluated

### I1 — Seed-host **isolate** rebuild (HEAD + two depth files) ⭐
**Shape:** Do not self-host. Do not emit the dirty 11-file tree.

1. Worktree or `$TMPDIR/s29c_iso/` copy of `ooda/oodac/` at **HEAD**
   (`52cc4b5`).
2. Overlay **only**:
   - `c_emit_print.oo` WT (Int `d`, 87→97) — 2.9 stmt belt
   - `c_emit_secret.oo` — **prefer I3 cherry-pick** (depth only). If DE
     will not split the hunk, overlay whole WT 231 L and **name** 7.10
     `str_slice` + 2.10 `__sec_sink__` as riders (not 2.9 FIXED).
3. Emit host = `bootstrap/seed/oodac` (fairy: secret **6s**, print OK,
   depth present in C).
4. `PURE_SKIP_CHECK=1 OODAC_BIN=<seed> bash scripts/oodac_pure_build.sh \
     oodac/main.oo $TMPDIR/s29c_oodac_depth`
   Same contract as `scripts/seed_pure_multi_smoke.sh` (side path).
5. Do **not** copy over `oodac/oodac` until I2 is green.

**Why this is the ship-now after rebuild-fail:** tree ELF cannot emit
`c_emit_secret.oo` (hang, HEAD **and** WT). Seed can. Isolate stops
`check_caps` / `OO_FLIGHT_RECORDER_LOG` / R2 / 6.1 from riding the 2.9
binary. `PURE_SKIP_CHECK=1` walks around R4 / AST deadlock on `main.oo`.

**Darwin:** Close 10 · Honest 10 · Smoke 9 · Entropy 10 · Ship 9 → **avg 9.6**

### I2 — Prove the **side** ELF (same rails, new host) ⭐
**Shape:** `OODAC_BIN=$TMPDIR/s29c_oodac_depth` + virgin TMPDIR cwd.

| Gate | Expect |
|------|--------|
| Fingerprint | **new** size / md5 / BuildID — not `a44ee35e…` / `a93cfd09…` |
| Runtime nm | check walker LPAREN **≥ 2**; scan_call **5** token eqs; stmt loop LPAREN (`s29c_runtime.oot` list) |
| H-later | `println((1), tok)` check **and** emit-c `ERR	secret` |
| H-same | `println(("x") + tok)` check **and** emit-c `ERR	secret`; **no** `oo_print_*` operand `tok` |
| Peer1 #3 | `eprintln(id(1), tok)` check **and** emit-c `ERR	secret` |
| Control | `println(n, tok)` still dual SECRET; `println("tok")` no-FP |
| Smoke | `s29_println_guard_smoke.sh` **exit 0** on **that** ELF |
| Grep | **no** `c_secret_emit_guard` in print/secret; **no** `args = args +` in `c_emit_println` |

`ERR	type` is FAIL. Then — and only then — replace gitignored
`oodac/oodac`. Do **not** `git add` the ELF.

**Darwin:** Close 9 · Honest 10 · Smoke 10 · Entropy 10 · Ship 9 → **avg 9.6**

### I3 — Cherry-pick **depth only** onto HEAD `c_emit_secret.oo`
**Shape:** HEAD file is 259 L first-`)`. Copy the two Int `depth`
counters (scan_call + println/eprintln loop). Leave HEAD sink-list
and **omit** WT 7.10 / 2.10 / compress. Print overlay is already a
14-line 2.9-only diff.

**Darwin:** Close 8 · Honest 10 · Smoke 8 · Entropy 9 · Ship 8 → **avg 8.6**  
**Why bundle with I1:** cleanest 2.9 binary. If cherry-pick slips,
I1 whole-file overlay + named riders is acceptable. Do **not** block
the ship on a pretty diff.

### I4 — Two-TU C splice (if isolate multi still fails)
**Shape:** Seed already emitted both TUs. Replace `c_emit_println` /
`c_secret_scan_call` / `check_secret_println_sinks` in a **HEAD**
seed `all.c`, gcc-link a side ELF.

**Darwin:** Close 8 · Honest 7 · Smoke 7 · Entropy 7 · Ship 6 → **avg 7.0**  
**Why fallback, not first:** works if `pure_build` of HEAD+two dies on
an unrelated module. Manual splice is easy to mis-cut. Prefer I1.

